WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.860
- It's very clear to me
that over the next 15 years,

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:05.030
what the blockchain will do,

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:08.000
especially in the NFT
form on top of Ethereum

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.700
is create a world that will
eat up all of the contracts,

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:13.533
all of them.

00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:17.020
Every contract over the
next 15 to 25 years,

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.010
will be done on the blockchain.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:21.860
Now, that doesn't eliminate
the need for what we do here,

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.475
but it definitely requires
for you to understand it.

00:00:25.475 --> 00:00:27.610
(upbeat music)
(man screaming)

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.583
- [Narrator] You've got your perspective.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.796
(crowds cheering)

00:00:32.796 --> 00:00:34.883
- I just wanna be happy,
don't you wanna be happy?

00:00:35.841 --> 00:00:37.660
(upbeat music)

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:38.981
Morning, Atlanta.

00:00:38.981 --> 00:00:42.382
(crowds cheering)

00:00:42.382 --> 00:00:44.963
It's really, really nice
to be with all of you.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.850
I don't have a ton of time on stage,

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:51.290
'cause I got to run to the meet and greet.

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:53.700
So, I wanna really get
into a bunch of things

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.950
that are on my mind for this sector.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:59.464
Try to bring as much value as
I can while we're together.

00:00:59.464 --> 00:01:03.930
I think much like two
years ago when I was here,

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.561
how many people were here for that?

00:01:05.561 --> 00:01:07.590
(crowds cheering)
Thank you.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:08.833
It's really interesting,

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.000
I really play in two very opposite places

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.300
when it comes to
business, life philosophy,

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.133
all of it really,

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:20.020
which is so much of what
I do and think about

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:22.150
and what I admire and see in others

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:25.040
is a remarkable level of consistency

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.680
of what is truly tried and true.

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:31.070
And then on the complete
other extreme part,

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.290
I really spend almost all my time,

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.620
trying to understand the one thing

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.340
that connects everybody in this room,

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.770
regardless of what
they're trying to achieve,

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:42.090
whether you're in this room

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.230
and under the context of this room,

00:01:44.230 --> 00:01:45.900
you're clearly trying to achieve something

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.900
from a professional lens.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:51.620
But the reality is if you're
passionate about fundraising

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:56.180
for your kid's school or if
you wanna segway your career

00:01:56.180 --> 00:01:58.330
or if you've got a side hustle

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:03.330
or if you decide to pivot
or run for public office,

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:05.400
there's just such a fascinating thing

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.200
that has always been true,

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.750
which is attention is the asset

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.420
and how you fill that attention,

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:16.190
becomes the variable of what happens.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:18.400
I was born in the Soviet Union

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.160
and came to the US when I was three

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.740
and grew up in the 80s
during the Cold War.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:28.300
And I've always wondered
if because of that,

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:32.430
I've always had an extra
interest in the media,

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:35.540
in propaganda, in communication,

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:38.330
because that was so much the
warfare of the Soviet Union

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:40.030
and the US and obviously
I don't have to explain

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:40.960
to anybody in this room.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.950
I think over the last half decade,

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:45.860
our society started paying
a lot more attention

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.900
to communication.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.800
I was always fascinated by why

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:51.810
if there was a coup in a country,

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.580
would they go to the TV station

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:56.620
and the newspapers even before
they went to the palace.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:57.940
And it made me always understand

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.980
that this shit is important.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.683
Communication is the variable.

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:05.736
What's really fascinating
about this industry.

00:03:05.736 --> 00:03:07.330
And I have many friends in it,

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:10.700
is when trying to grow the business,

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:14.260
most of the DNA in this room is sales DNA,

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.200
it's not brand DNA.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.540
You're not marketing, you're selling.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.320
It's why Google does so well.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.670
It's why so many people
here feel comfortable,

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:25.300
allocating money to Google AdWords,

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.920
because it's transactional.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.710
Somebody types something in,

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:31.800
you spend dollars on
it, you go to the top,

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:36.340
you see and feel the ROI very quickly.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:37.440
I understand it.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.750
I love selling stuff.

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.320
It's very easy to understand.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.670
It's very easy to invest in.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:47.790
What's impossibly difficult
to invest in is brand.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:49.210
It's hard.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:51.920
Why am I wearing these?

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:53.690
Because a brand,

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:55.757
nobody knocked on my fucken door and said,

00:03:55.757 --> 00:03:57.497
"Do you wanna buy these Nike's?"

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:01.050
I didn't type in Nike into it and then,

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:02.210
this is brand.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:05.600
This little swoosh is
worth a trillion dollars,

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.150
a trillion.

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:08.630
And so I think about that,

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:11.320
because it's easier to
understand with Nike,

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:14.340
but it's harder for a lot
of people in this room

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:16.740
to think about it from
their business lens,

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.220
though, we see it.

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:19.120
Many of you know,

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:21.980
many of you have your
faces on billboards and ads

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:24.320
and newspapers and things of that nature.

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.740
I believe in all that,

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:28.590
I just don't believe in
overpaying for yesterday

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:30.133
and not investing in today.

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:34.770
Like, whatever you did to
get here was about attention.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:37.030
Whether it was shaking hands

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:40.020
and having friends and
working the local thing,

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:44.200
whether word of mouth is just attention.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:47.440
You did something for Craig
and he liked it enough.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:49.760
And when Sally asked him, he referred,

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.520
it's all just the same game.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:52.890
The problem is

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.410
and the thing that I have
had an enormous amount

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:59.560
of passion on is if attention is the asset

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:00.900
that grows everything,

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.710
that creates the result,

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:07.710
why aren't people interested
in investing the 20 hours

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:11.890
that it would take to understand

00:05:11.890 --> 00:05:16.010
the current space of attention?

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:18.110
Like I just don't understand why

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:23.110
you wouldn't see through the
curiosity and spend five hours

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:26.700
to understand why a TikTok
video might actually lead

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:27.533
to a customer.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:31.129
I don't understand why you would say no,

00:05:31.129 --> 00:05:32.210
let me rephrase it.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:34.110
I very much understand why you say no.

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:35.783
You say no,

00:05:35.783 --> 00:05:38.550
because you positioned it in
your head as something else.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.480
You've positioned it as the thing

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:43.700
that your kids spend all
their time on, right?

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:46.480
But what you don't do is the homework

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:49.940
that makes you understand
that over the last 18 months,

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:52.790
the growth of 35 to 55 year olds on TikTok

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:53.890
is so extraordinary,

00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:56.030
we haven't seen growth
of consumption like that,

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:57.763
since 2011 Facebook.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:01.010
All of a sudden, if you
understand that truth,

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:04.080
it at least leads to the curiosity.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.840
How many people here are
producing three pieces

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.860
of TikTok video a day for their business.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:09.693
And if you raised your hand,

00:06:09.693 --> 00:06:12.209
I'm gonna check on stage
publicly, so don't lie.

00:06:12.209 --> 00:06:14.540
(crowd laughing)

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:17.120
How many people in this entire room,

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:19.820
make three TikTok videos
a day for their company?

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:20.683
Raise your hands,

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:22.393
two.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:25.313
I'm sorry, three, sorry, Sally.

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:28.600
Three, three.

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:30.650
I love it and I love the passion of that.

00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:34.040
What excites me about that

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.880
is because I've been
making content about TikTok

00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:38.490
for two and a half years,

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:43.490
I already have dozens of emails
from lawyers, contractors,

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:48.990
a cement provider hit me up last week

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:52.060
that he landed a big
contract from a TikTok.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:53.700
Do you know how insane it sounds

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:57.290
to even say that a cement provider,

00:06:57.290 --> 00:07:00.650
landed a six-figure
contract from a TikTok?

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:05.240
Even for me as progressive
and curious and in it as I am,

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:08.060
I understand how far
fetched that may feel,

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.440
but it's a reality.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:10.860
And this isn't a talk to say,

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:13.250
everybody run out and go make TikToks.

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:14.540
This is a talk of,

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:18.570
are you challenging yourself
to do branding work?

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:23.303
Because it's the singular
thing that grows anything.

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:27.740
Branding is the singular
thing that grows anything.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:29.070
It's just the way the world works.

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:32.433
And so, I think the
opportunity is extraordinary.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:35.890
One more time by show of hands,

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:40.890
by show of hands how many people
produce two original videos

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:45.000
or written articles a day on LinkedIn?

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:45.833
Raise your hand.

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:52.090
One, one, two, got you.

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:53.200
Two,

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:58.200
again, that one I struggle with way more,

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:02.820
but it goes back to my only
interest in this talk today.

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:06.360
Why are we, the world,

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:08.420
this is not just this
sector, this is the world.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:11.810
Why are we not interested

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:14.850
in putting in the 20 to 30 hours

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:19.010
to understand something
that's happening today?

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:20.610
LinkedIn for the last four years

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:23.800
has converted itself into
being the business Facebook.

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:26.360
This is not the LinkedIn
we all grew up with.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:29.300
LinkedIn Marketing isn't
spamming people on email.

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:31.370
It is making content to go in the feed.

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:33.720
How many people here
consume content on LinkedIn

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.560
and know what I'm referring
to raise your hands,

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:36.393
raise it high.

00:08:36.393 --> 00:08:39.200
Please, I want you to
raise it higher, come on.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.033
Look.

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:44.820
That is the fun thing for me.

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:47.230
Almost half this room is consuming it.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:49.370
Two people are making for it.

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:51.850
It speaks to the thing I
started this talk with.

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:54.400
I believe this room is
in the sales business

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.430
and I believe if you can make the shift

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:59.720
to understanding that you
need to be in the marketing

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:00.730
and brand business,

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:04.410
it's the only thing that
can substantially double,

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:07.330
triple, 10X a business, it's real.

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:08.163
It's what happens.

00:09:08.163 --> 00:09:09.360
It happens at every business,

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:10.920
it's happened for the last 20 years

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:14.393
as we've lived through
the internet revolution.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:17.700
This is important talk

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:21.913
for a much more important
reason for this specific room.

00:09:23.370 --> 00:09:25.500
The reason it's an
important talk for this room

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:30.500
is if you became an operator
of contemporary marketing

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:33.693
for your business in this room,

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:39.280
you would start the process
of changing your perspective

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:41.560
on how you navigate your business life,

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:44.340
which is about to become
unbelievably important

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:46.030
to everybody in this room,

00:09:46.030 --> 00:09:48.593
because of the advent of the blockchain.

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:52.810
As we are going into this next tier,

00:09:52.810 --> 00:09:55.100
I think all of us
looking around this room,

00:09:55.100 --> 00:09:58.610
man, this is a perfect
age demo for the most part

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:02.710
of many people either
never knowing anything else

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:05.290
or the majority of the
room based on what I see,

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:08.930
many of us remembering the
world before the internet

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:11.380
and watching what it's
done over the last 25 years

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:13.080
to change our society.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:15.810
How many people here made
it through high school,

00:10:15.810 --> 00:10:17.290
without being on the internet?

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:18.360
Raise your hands.

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:19.193
I'll raise mine,

00:10:19.193 --> 00:10:20.460
raise it high,

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:23.115
that's right kids it sucked.

00:10:23.115 --> 00:10:26.570
(crowd laughing)

00:10:26.570 --> 00:10:29.010
So, it's a lot of hands in this room.

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:32.463
We recall the world changed a lot.

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:36.710
The world's changed a
lot in the last 25 years.

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:38.420
The biggest companies
of the world changed,

00:10:38.420 --> 00:10:39.950
consumer behaviors changed,

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:41.450
the way we buy things has changed,

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:44.100
the decisions we make changed.

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:48.610
And now we have decentralized
servers brewing.

00:10:48.610 --> 00:10:49.710
And I'm sure at this point,

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:52.120
especially because this
has been the year of NFTs

00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:53.400
and Bitcoin,

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:56.290
most people at this point have heard

00:10:56.290 --> 00:11:00.060
of the blockchain, Bitcoin, NFTs,

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:01.320
but I'm also empathetic

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:03.750
that most people have not
spent their 20 to 50 hours

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:05.340
to really understand it.

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:07.200
But let me give you a simple statement

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:09.240
that I genuinely believe will be true

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:12.200
and I think has a lot to
do with this industry.

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:14.340
If with one is to
understand the blockchain.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:16.700
And in 1995 when I saw the internet,

00:11:16.700 --> 00:11:19.820
I realized that my dad's
one liquor store needed

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:21.550
to be an internet retailer,

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:23.280
'cause that's how I was gonna
help my family business.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.980
And even though I didn't own a computer,

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:27.340
I launched one of the first
e-commerce businesses.

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:29.050
And then I did it again with social

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:31.630
and that's kind of how I've navigated.

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:35.340
It is very clear to me that
over the next 15 years,

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:36.500
what the blockchain will do,

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:39.480
especially in the NFT
form on top of Ethereum

00:11:39.480 --> 00:11:44.180
is create a world that will
eat up all of the contracts,

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.013
all of them.

00:11:45.013 --> 00:11:48.500
Every contract over the
next 15 to 25 years,

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:50.490
will be done on the blockchain.

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:53.350
Now, that doesn't eliminate
the need for what we do here,

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:56.763
but it definitely requires
for you to understand it.

00:11:58.120 --> 00:11:59.673
And so for me,

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:03.200
this talk is kind of really interesting,

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:05.390
because it reminds me of a talk,

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:07.040
a little bit of a different timing,

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:12.040
but I gave a talk to the
limo and car industry,

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:15.410
right as Uber was happening.

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:17.490
And the majority of my talk was about Uber

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:18.890
in the first 15 minutes.

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:20.290
And as you can imagine,

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:21.540
the crowd didn't like it.

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:26.060
And I was telling them
that I was concerned,

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:27.950
because the iPhone had
become the remote control

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:30.530
of our society and now it really is.

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:34.480
And that I thought it was
dangerous and people poo-pooed it.

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:37.490
They said that legally,

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:40.040
